I've been meaning to do it eventually, hoping someone else will get to it
first (I don't even have enough time to *play* NetHack at the moment).

If you want to patch it, the code is in drawing.c, in the
"assign_rogue_graphics" function.  You might want to also peek at the
IBM_r_oc_syms array defined just above, and the comments and ifdefs
therein.  As far as I know, the only problem on *nix (MSDOS not defined) is
the smiley face char assigned in drawing.c.  I have no idea what happens on
windows versions with MSDOS defined; in this case most of the chars in the
IBM_r_oc_syms array will be below 0x20, and some terms (PuTTY?) may refuse
to print them.

The patch might be as simple as sticking another 
"#if defined(MSDOS)...#endif", or some other set of defs,  around the line
monsyms[S_HUMAN] = 0x01; /* smiley face */

